Error: hex #99 is not in this city's known catchment; see keryx city
Usage:
  build [city] [flags]

Examples:
  keryx build --list
  keryx build --type farm --hex 3,-1          # farm/mine/lumbermill/stonequarry are hex-bound: pick a catchment hex
  keryx build --type harbour          # requires coastal (adjacent sea hex)
  keryx build --type mine --hex 5,2 --province <province-id>   # build in a colony
  keryx build --type winery           # produces nothing unless a hills/plains/scrub_maquis tile is in catchment
  keryx build --queue                 # see what's already queued, with cancel-build IDs

Flags:
      --province string   province ID to build in (default: your capital)
  -t, --type string       building type (omit to see list)
      --god string        the god a temple is built for (one temple per god and city): potnia, velchanos, asterion, sea_daimons_stillness
      --hex string        catchment q,r or ordinal 6/#6 — required for hex-bound building types
      --list              show the building catalogue and exit
      --queue             show this settlement's build queue (with queue IDs for cancel-build) and exit
  -h, --help              help for build

Error: the lumbermill is a hex building — staff it with: keryx place timber 6 +2 (hex #6)
Usage:
  staff <byggnad> [+n|-n] [flags]

Examples:
  keryx staff shipyard +1
  keryx staff temple +1 --god potnia
  keryx staff olive_press
  keryx staff olive_press +2
  keryx staff olive_press -1 --province <prov-id>

Flags:
      --god string        which temple, when the city has one to several gods
  -h, --help              help for staff
      --province string   province ID/name (default: your capital)

Selected world one
Error: a Nomadic Host founds its metropolis with keryx founding settle --name <name> (add --yes to confirm)
Usage:
  unit march [flags]

Examples:
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --q 5 --r -3
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --target 5,-3
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --q 5 --r -3 --stance fortify
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --q 5 --r -3 --intent colonize --name Thapsos --yes
  # Colonize the hex the unit already stands on (no coords needed):
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --intent colonize --name Thapsos --yes
  # Any march reveals fog along its route toward a frontier coordinate:
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --q 12 --r -8
  # Explore an area for 12 game days, then automatically return home
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --q 12 --r -8 --intent explore --ticks 12
  # Land troops from a laden ship in port, then sail home on its own:
  keryx unit march --unit <ship-id> --q 20 --r -5 --intent land
  # ...and found a colony there with no further order:
  keryx unit march --unit <ship-id> --q 20 --r -5 --intent land --colonize --name Thapsos
  # Attack an enemy settlement and annex it instead of the sack default:
  keryx unit march --unit <id> --q 5 --r -3 --mode annex

Flags:
      --colonize        with --intent land: found a colony on arrival with no further order (use --name to name it)
      --confirm         send the order after the hiketeia warning (attacking a fallen Wanax's risen host)
  -h, --help            help for march
      --intent string   arrival intent: colonize (found a new colony — use --name to name it; omit --q/--r to colonize the hex the unit is on) | explore (first to the selected hex, then explores around it; turns home by half the chosen duration) | land (a laden ship in port lands its cargo on an unclaimed land hex, then sails home on its own; add --colonize to found a colony there)
      --mode string     conquest choice when attacking a settlement: sack (default, loot+raze) | annex (take the city)
      --name string     colony name (with --intent colonize, or --intent land --colonize)
      --preview         estimate arrival without sending an order
      --q int           target hex Q — axial coordinate, read it off 'keryx map' (required, unless colonizing in place or using --target)
      --r int           target hex R — axial coordinate, read it off 'keryx map' (required, unless colonizing in place or using --target)
      --stance string   stance on arrival: fortify|storm|sentry
      --target string   target hex as q,r — alternative to --q/--r (e.g. 5,-3)
      --ticks int       explore duration in game days (omit for server default)
      --to string       known city name as destination — alternative to --q/--r or --target
      --unit string     unit UUID (required)
      --yes             skip the colonize catchment-forecast confirmation (required for non-interactive/agent use)

